{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-202883-r4505265","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Texas Style Barbecue Ribs","sourcePageId":202883,"sourceRevision":"4505265","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-10T01:15:43Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Texas%20Style%20Barbecue%20Ribs&oldid=4505265","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T16:18:16.807Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Barbecue recipes","Category:Main course recipes","Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes using cayenne","Category:Recipes using chile flake","Category:Recipes using dark brown sugar","Category:Recipes using honey","Category:Recipes using pork","Category:Recipes using vinegar","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings","Category:Smoked recipes","Category:Texas recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"d95ffae76c9a54fc11ecd9c7287b4a059904cf5c6f72eb5adf1d86e9a59f388a","sourceWikitext":"__NOTOC__{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Meat recipes\n| Difficulty = 3\n}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Texas cuisine|Texas cuisine]]\n== Ingredients ==\n\n=== '''Mop''' ===\n\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] apple [[Cookbook:Cider Vinegar|cider vinegar]]\n* ⅓ cup [[Cookbook:Honey|honey]]\n* ¼ cup [[Cookbook:Worcestershire Sauce|Worcestershire sauce]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] [[Cookbook:Cayenne Pepper|cayenne pepper]]\n\n=== '''Rub''' ===\n\n* 6 tbsp dark [[Cookbook:Brown Sugar|brown sugar]]\n* 2 tbsp cayenne pepper\n* 2 tbsp smoked [[Cookbook:Paprika|paprika]]\n* 2 tbsp kosher [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n* 2 tbsp freshly ground [[Cookbook:Pepper|black pepper]]\n* 2 tbsp [[Cookbook:Old Bay|Old Bay]] seasoning\n* 1 tbsp [[Cookbook:Red pepper flakes|red pepper flakes]]\n* 2 tbsp [[Cookbook:Garlic Powder|garlic powder]]\n* 2 tbsp [[Cookbook:Onion Powder|onion powder]]\n* 2 tbsp dried [[Cookbook:Rosemary|rosemary]]\n* 2 tbsp dried [[Cookbook:Thyme|thyme]]\n\n=== Other ===\n\n* 2 slabs St. Louis style [[Cookbook:Pork|pork]] ribs\n\n== Procedure ==\n#Combine all Mop ingredients and place in a spray bottle. Combine all Rub ingredients and massage into pork. Refrigerate pork overnight.\n#The next day, place hickory chunks into the firebox of a smoker. Heat to 225°F.\n#Place ribs in smoker and cook, spraying with Mop often.\n#[[Cookbook:Grilling|Grill]] ribs on high, turning often, spraying grilled side every time it's turned, until well browned on both sides.\n#Remove and let rest 7 minutes.\n#Slice into one rib portions and place in a large stainless steel bowl. Pour in about ½ cup of Mop and [[Cookbook:Mixing#Tossing|toss]] to coat ribs. Serve warm.\n\n[[Category:Texas recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using pork]]\n[[Category:Barbecue recipes]]\n[[Category:Smoked recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using vinegar]]\n[[Category:Main course recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using dark brown sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chile flake]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cayenne]]\n[[Category:Recipes using honey]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Texas Style Barbecue Ribs","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1 cup apple cider vinegar","sourceText":"1 cup apple cider vinegar","amountText":"1 cup apple cid